  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Satendra Yadav @ Tillu And 2 Others vs State Of U.P. on 20 May, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ? In Chamber Case :- Criminal Misc Anticipatory Bail Application U/S 438 Cr.P.C. No. - 2608 of 2020 Applicant :- Satendra Yadav @ Tillu And 2 Others Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Yogesh Kumar Mishra,Navin Kumar Sharma Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J. Order on Criminal Misc. Exemption Application Application is allowed. Order on Criminal Misc. Anticipatory Bail Application",
    "facts": "Submission is that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicants under section 272, 273 I.P.C. is unjustified. Offence under section 60(A) of Excise Act is bailable and trible by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. Without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case and considering the nature of accusation and his antecedents, the applicants are entitled to be released on bail in this case.",
